          "level": "preferred",
          "summary": "Raise IBM's cap to the greater of USD 1,000,000 or 12 months' charges, delete the data-loss exclusion and add Excluded Claims carve-outs.",
          "comment": "[Playbook] We can accept a mutual cap, but it must be meaningful: the greater of 12 months' charges or USD 1,000,000, and IBM cannot exclude liability for loss of our records or data when it hosts them. Confidentiality, data protection/security, indemnification, gross negligence, wilful misconduct, fraud and IP infringement sit outside the cap.",
          "ops": [
            {
              "kind": "replace",
              "paragraphId": "p0112",
              "oldText": "up to the greater of $100,000 or the charges paid by Customer to IBM for the Services in the twelve (12) months immediately preceding the accrual of the first claim related to the Services.",
              "newText": "up to the greater of $1,000,000 or the charges paid or payable by Customer to IBM for the Services in the twelve (12) months immediately preceding the accrual of the first claim related to the Services."
            },
            {
              "kind": "insert_after",
              "paragraphId": "p0113",
              "text": "The foregoing limitations do not apply to Excluded Claims. \"Excluded Claims\" means a party's breach of its confidentiality, data protection or security obligations, its indemnification obligations, its gross negligence, wilful misconduct or fraud, and its infringement of the other party's intellectual property rights."
            },
            {
              "kind": "delete_paragraph",
              "paragraphId": "p0114"
            }
          ]
        },
