          "ruleId": "INDEMN",
          "level": "preferred",
          "summary": "Extend IBM's indemnity beyond IP to breach of law, data breach and gross negligence/wilful misconduct, and narrow Customer's indemnity for Services Recipient claims.",
          "comment": "[Playbook] IBM's indemnity is IP-only while ours covers any claim by a Services Recipient \"related, directly or indirectly, to the Services\". We have added IBM's standard indemnity limbs (breach of law, data breach, gross negligence/wilful misconduct) and deleted the open-ended Customer limb.",
          "ops": [
            {
              "kind": "insert_after",
              "paragraphId": "p0096",
              "text": "In addition to and notwithstanding the foregoing, IBM will defend, indemnify and hold harmless Customer, its Enterprise and their respective employees, officers, agents and directors from and against any third-party claim, and all resulting damages, costs and expenses (including reasonable attorneys' fees), to the extent arising out of (a) IBM's breach of applicable law; (b) any unauthorized access to or disclosure of Content or Customer data caused by IBM; or (c) IBM's gross negligence or wilful misconduct."
